From: Oliphaunt Maintainers <dev@oliphaunt.dev>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] oliphaunt-wasix: default WAL sync to fdatasync

WASIX libc defines O_DSYNC, so PostgreSQL's generic platform selection chooses
open_datasync.  Wasmer-backed filesystems do not provide one portable
open-time synchronization contract, while WASIX exposes an explicit
fd_datasync operation.

Select fdatasync in the shared WASIX port header.  Browser and Rust Wasmer
hosts then use the same PostgreSQL-owned durability default without a
language-binding startup override, while an explicit PostgreSQL configuration
can still select another supported method.
---
 src/include/port/wasix-dl.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/include/port/wasix-dl.h b/src/include/port/wasix-dl.h
--- a/src/include/port/wasix-dl.h
+++ b/src/include/port/wasix-dl.h
@@ -6,6 +6,12 @@
 #ifndef PG_PORT_WASIX_DL_H
 #define PG_PORT_WASIX_DL_H
 
+/*
+ * Prefer WASIX's explicit fd_datasync operation over an O_DSYNC open flag,
+ * whose persistence semantics vary across Wasmer-backed filesystems.
+ */
+#define PLATFORM_DEFAULT_WAL_SYNC_METHOD WAL_SYNC_METHOD_FDATASYNC
+
 #if defined(OLIPHAUNT_WASM_SINGLE_USER) || defined(OLIPHAUNT_WASM_SIDE_MODULE)
 #include <setjmp.h>
 #endif
-- 
